US-018 (Asset Registry) is implemented and every quality gate I was able to run passes. The only remaining item is the ASan/UBSan preset, which I did not run (details below).

**What was built**, in a new `engine_assets` library under `engine/assets/`:
- **Registry** (`AssetRegistry`): one record per GUID holding the source path, importer type, canonical importer settings, SHA-256 content hash, and sorted dependency GUIDs. It rejects nil GUIDs, GUID and path conflicts, absolute or `.` paths, empty importers, and self-dependencies. It also provides removal (which reports dependents), path-only moves, dependents, missing dependencies, and a cycle-safe dependency closure.
- **Project scan** (`scan_project`): reads `<source>.meta` sidecars, which are the only place a GUID is stored. A moved or renamed source keeps its GUID. A copy with its sidecar fails as a GUID conflict. The scan is all-or-nothing, so a bad sidecar leaves nothing behind. `create_asset_metadata` writes a new sidecar atomically.
- **SHA-256** (`ContentHash`), checked against FIPS vectors at the padding boundaries.
- **Fixture project** (`tests/fixtures/assets/registry_project`, with a Cyrillic source name). Integration tests copy it to a scratch directory per case and cover deletion, renaming, moving a folder, orphaned sidecars, GUID conflicts, malformed sidecars, and metadata creation.

